WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:13.620
Sup y’all?

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.550
Grab yo’ tissues and pop some Zoloft cuz
today we weepin’ like a bunch of bitches

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:24.980
with Where the Red Fern Grows by Wilson Rawls.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.029
Billy Coleman rollin home from work one day
when he see a dog fight goin down in the streets:

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.739
a whole gang of em jumpin a Redbone hound.

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:37.460
Afta’ shakin’ dem haters off, Billy take
dat pooch back to the crib to give it some

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:38.460
love and care.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.500
Dat puppy chill-sesh throw us in to a FLASHBACK,
playa!

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.320
Back when Billy was a lil ‘un, he was hittin’
his parents up fo’ a dog.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.320
Pops like “Aight, son.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.179
We’ll get you a lil pup from the neighbor’s
place.”

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:56.519
But Billy like “Bitch please, I want two
redbone hounds so I can hunt coons.”

00:00:56.519 --> 00:00:57.519
That’s RA-coons!!

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:00.179
And daddy all like: “Da hell you think this
is boy?

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:01.769
We ain’t got da ends fo’ dat.”

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:07.710
So Billy hustle fo’ TWO DAMN YEARS til he
save up enough cheddar to buy a couple dogs,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.220
and his gramps help him order em.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.090
When the dogs come in, Billy hear he gonna
have to wait a week before he gets em.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.240
But Billy ain’t gonna just sit on his ass
and wait, so he hikes 20 miles ONE WAY to

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.390
scoop em up.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:24.310
Billy end up gettin’ one boy puppy and one
girl puppy, and since it’s gettin late,

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.439
decide to set up shop in a cave and hold it
down til morning.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:33.030
When a mountain lion roll up tryna mad dog
em, da pups don’t take NO shit and start

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:38.039
hollerin’ right back “WOOF WOOF MUTHAFUCKA”.

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:42.880
Billy start screamin his ass off and throwin
rocks til eventually dat puss turns his ass

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.420
around and book it.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.670
Next day, Billy leave da cave and peep two
names written on a tree and decide THAT’S

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.649
gonna be the dem pooches names: Old Dan and
Lil’ Ann.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:58.549
Back at home, Billy’s gramps help a brutha
catch a coon, and then use da fur to teach

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:01.829
Ol’ Dan and Lil’ Anne how to HUNT like
BIG DAWGS.

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:06.479
Billy recognize dat Old Dan got da muscle,
but it’s Lil’ Anne who got da brains.

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.190
One da first day of hunting season, Old Dan
and Lil’ Anne chase a coon up da phattest

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.190
tree in town.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.680
Billy promised his pups dat once they cornered
one of dem suckas, he’d do the rest.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.570
So B-money bust his ass for DAYS tryna’
cut dat tree down.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:25.000
Jus’ when he bout to say “fuck it,”
he get down on his knees and start prayin’

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.080
fo mo’ strength..

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.590
Then what do ya know?

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:32.080
WHOOOOOSH- a big ass wind blows the tree down
and the pups GIT dat coon.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.680
As da months go on, word on the street is
dat Billy and his pups are da best hunters

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.680
in da hood.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.240
Knowin he got da game sowed up, Grandpa make
a bet with da local Pritchard boys sayin dat

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.790
Old Dan and Lil Ann so trill that they can
even catch the mysterious “ghost coon.”

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.720
And jus’ like the G-UNIT they be, Billy
and the dogs pretty much CATCH it, but Billy

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.060
don’t wanna kill da poor thang- he just
feelin’ sorry for it.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.930
When Rubin Prichard gettin’ all up in Billy’s
grill fo’ bitchin’ out, Lil Anne and Old

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.990
Dan start whoopin on Rubin’s pooch.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:07.320
Rubin grabs an axe to fight off the dogs,
but he chokes and accidentally ices himself.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.900
Later, gramps enters Billy and the pooches
in to a hunting competition.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.670
Not only do Lil’ Anne win “sexiest bitch
in town”, but after nights of roughin it

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.340
through a redonkulous blizzard, the pups bring
home the GOLD CUP.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.900
Now Billy and his fam are 3 Benjamins richer
too.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.290
Later, Billy on da hunt when Ol’ Dan and
Lil’ Anne corner a damn mountain lion in

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.290
a tree.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.340
When da Mountain Lion start scrappin’ with
da pups, Billy grab an axe ready to bang out.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.090
But it’s the dogs who gotta save Billy’s
weak ass.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:41.460
They eventually kill the Mountain Lion, but
Old Dan gets fucked up in da fight, and dies.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:46.320
Lil Anne can’t go on without her puppy-bro,
so she stops eating and dies too.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.320
Man.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.320
Fuck this book.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.320
I’m done.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.320
I’m done.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.610
(Sparky walks off screen) Billy just cain’t
figger out why his pups had to die.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.510
And you know what?

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.510
Me neither.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.510
Bullshit, man.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:02.540
Ain’t all bad though, with dat swole stack
o’ prize money, Billy’s family can finally

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.410
get outta da boonies and move to da city.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:10.270
On the day of the move, Billy visits the dogs
graves, where dere be some red fern growin.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.500
Brutha get all riled up and bout to chop it
down, but then he remember dat according to

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:19.620
Native American legend, only angels can plant
dat shit and dat it last forever.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.970
So he decide to leave it, knowin’ dat he
ain’t never gonna forget da way those dogs

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.490
affected him fo’ the better.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:33.259
Mah boy Edgar Allen Poe once preached dat
there ain’t nuthin’ mo depressing than

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.669
losin’ a lover.

00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:36.419
Guess dat fool never lost a dog.

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:37.949
...Yeah I cried.

00:04:37.949 --> 00:04:39.050
SO WHAT??

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:43.710
Like Billy himself say on page 16, da love
between a man and his pooch ain’t like da

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:47.360
feeling you get when mackin’ on a hunny
tryna get some action.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.580
Nuh-uh.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.600
This is some of da realest love in the game.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.960
Them dogs keep it so real that they willing
to lay it ALL on the line to get their boy

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.949
Billy’s back- and it ain’t just cuz they
loyal.

00:04:58.949 --> 00:05:06.060
Check what Mr. Kyle say on p. 184

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:23.450
And it ain’t jus’ Ol’ Dan and Lil’
Anne gooin hard fo’ Billy.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:28.639
Matta’ fact, Billy show dat kinda love ain’t
a one way street: he ALSO grindin hard in

00:05:28.639 --> 00:05:29.639
the name of love.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:34.659
When da pups run a coon up dat big ass tree,
Billy gonna do what he promised- cut dat tree

00:05:34.659 --> 00:05:37.949
even if it take him a damn year of sweatin’
his balls off to do it.

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:42.689
And you best BELIEVE he follow through, cuz
Billy is one of the most DETERMINED cats in

00:05:42.689 --> 00:05:43.689
da hood.

00:05:43.689 --> 00:05:47.620
Whether it be hustlin to stack enough cheddar
to buy the dogs, or teachin’ em to swim-

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.599
Billy neva’ trippin in the face of a gnarly
challenge.

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:52.419
He just beast through it like a G.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:55.999
But sometimes, determination ain’t cuttin’
it fo’ Billy.

00:05:55.999 --> 00:05:57.280
He need somethin’ mo.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.009
A buncha times throughout this book, Billy
start prayin’ fo strength, and after he

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:05.009
do, he able to keep it clutch and get shit
DONE.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:10.259
And just as God pitied Billy and decided to
help a brutha out when he in need, Billy always

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:15.009
showin’ love to otha’s when they in bunk-ass
situations- like when he told he gotta ghost

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:18.729
da ghost coon, he pities da poor thang and
tells Pritchard to step.

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:23.810
When da big man upstairs shows you love, ain’t
no doubt it’s legit to pay it forward.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:28.259
But when you lose somebody or something that
mean mo’ than life itself, how you gonna

00:06:28.259 --> 00:06:29.699
keep da faith?

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:33.800
Maybe yo prayers don’t always get answered
da way you want em to, but that don’t mean

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.819
da big G-man ain’t lookin’ out for you
in other ways.

00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:39.229
Peep this convo between Billy and his dad-

00:06:39.229 --> 00:07:07.449
All deez fresh themes- love, sacrifice, pity,
and God, come together in da image Red Fern

00:07:07.449 --> 00:07:09.550
that growin on dem dogs’ graves.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:14.620
Word is dat only angels can plant summodat
red stuff and it last fo’eva- jus’ like

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.900
the memory of Lil Anne and Ol’ Dan inside
Billy’s dome.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:22.599
And like he say at the beginning of the book,
after all these years, Billy feel like a piece

00:07:22.599 --> 00:07:24.360
of him still buried under dat fern.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:29.169
Yuh, this is a kids book, but it force us
to stare down the barrel of one of da realest

00:07:29.169 --> 00:07:52.710
questions they is: is there anything you love
enough 

00:07:52.710 --> 00:08:04.009
to give yo’ life for?

00:08:04.009 --> 00:08:23.250
Thanks for checkin me out, son.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:35.560
Catch y’all lata.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:39.669
Peace.

